      "Language": "ita",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "1436 cases of recent abdominal pain encountered in the Casualty Department of Biella Hospital over 18 consecutive months are examined. The incidence of the various abdominal pathologies, the diagnostic and therapeutic procedures adopted in the first hours after admission and any differences between original diagnosis by the general practitioner of the First Aid post, diagnosis on admission and diagnosis on release from hospital are examined."},
